00). Here S and B represent prefill length and batch size, respectively.\n\nTable 4: Results of Our Backend\n\n## A.3 COMPARISON WITH MLC-LLM RESULTS\n\nWe compare the results of SnapKV based self-speculation on MLC-LLM and our backend. As the measurement methods are different, we put them in two tables as shown in Table 4 and 5. The verification time of MLC-LLM includes one step of draft decode time. Our backend is highly optimized for speculative decoding setting, minimizing the drafting and verification overhead, thus, leading to better speedup. However, the trend that speedup increases with batch size is the same, aligning with our theoretical analysis in Section 3.","p":14,"l":"","box":[171,597,826,624]},{"r":10330,"c":21,"text":"<table border=\"1\"><tr><td>Target</td><td>Backend</td><td>Task</td><td>GPU</td><td>Prefill</td><td>Bsz</td><td>$\\gamma$</td><td>$\\gamma\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{D}}(1)$</td><td>$\\mathrm{T}_{V}(\\gamma)$</td><td>$\\Omega(\\gamma,\\alpha)$</td><td>$\\mathrm{T}^{\\mathrm{AR}}$</td><td>$\\mathrm{T}^{\\mathrm{SD}}$</td><td>x</td></tr><tr><td>Llama3.1-8B</td><td>Ours</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>16</td><td>3</td><td>10.96</td><td>6.91</td><td>3.42</td><td>6.41</td><td>5.41</td><td>1.18</td></tr><tr><td>Llama3.1-8B</td><td>Ours</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>32</td><td>4</td><td>16.69</td><td>10.39</td><td>4.10</td><td>9.23</td><td>6.75</td><td>1.37</td></tr><tr><td>Llama3.1-8B</td><td>Ours</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>64</td><td>5</td><td>23.96</td><td>17.45</td><td>4.59</td><td>14.85</td><td>9.17</td><td>1.62</td></tr></table>","p":14,"l":"","box":[190,777,808,825]},{"r":10331,"c":0,"text":"Table 5: Results of MLC-LLM\n\n<table border=\"1\"><tr><td>Target</td><td>Backend</td><td>Task</td><td>GPU</td><td>Prefill</td><td>Bsz</td><td>$\\gamma$</td><td>TD(1)</td><td>TV($\\gamma$)</td><td>NumGen</td><td>ARTrput</td><td>SDTrput</td><td>x</td></tr><tr><td>Llama3.1-8B</td><td>MLC-LLM</