><td>32</td><td>2</td><td>16.72</td><td>20.87</td><td>2.31</td><td>19.43</td><td>16.27</td><td>1.19</td></tr><tr><td>Qwen-2.5-32B</td><td>Qwen-2.5-7B(Streaming)</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>6.77</td><td>11.31<","p":15,"l":""},{"r":10348,"c":17,"text":"00</td><td>32000</td><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>6.77</td><td>11.31</td><td>2.27</td><td>10.42</td><td>7.97</td><td>1.31</td></tr><tr><td>Qwen-2.5-32B</td><td>Qwen-2.5-7B(Streaming)</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>16</td><td>2</td><td>7.21</td><td>14.59</td><td>2.26</td><td>13.36</td><td>9.64</td><td>1.39</td></tr><tr><td>Qwen-2.5-32B</td><td>Qwen-2.5-7B(Streaming)</td><td>PG-19</td><td>8xH100</td><td>32000</td><td>32</td><td>3</td><td>11.78</td><td>21.82</td><td>2.62</td><td>19.43</td><td>12","p":15,"l":""},{"r":10349,"c":18,"text":"td><td>11.78</td><td>21.82</td><td>2.62</td><td>19.43</td><td>12.85</td><td>1.51</td></tr></table>","p":15,"l":""},{"r":10350,"c":0,"text":"## A.6 TINYLLAMA1.1B-LLAMA2-7B-32K RESULTS\n\nWe also test the non-GQA model LLaMA-2-7B-32K for both StreamingLLM-based self-speculation and small draft model with StreamingLLM KV cache. Due to the lower FLOPS to memory ratio of non-GQA model, it tends to achieve higher speedup than GQA model under the same setting.\n\n(a) Draft: TinyLLama-1.1B , Target: LLaMA-2- 7B-32K\n\nPrefill 4000 ⚬ Prefill 16000 ⚬ Prefill 24000 ⚬ Prefill 32000\n\n⚬ Prefill 8000\n\n(b) Draft: StreamingLLM based KV. Target: LLaMA-2 -7B-32K\n\nFigure 9: End-to-end speedups for StreamingLLM-based self-speculation across various compressed KV budgets (left: 256, right: 512) on PG-19. Annotations indicate $\\gamma_{\\mathrm{optimal}}$ , which is the value corresponding to the highest speedup achieved. Experiments are conducted on 8xA100 with 8-way tensor parallelism. Raw data can be found in A.2.","p":16,"l":"","box":[172,104,527,119]}]}